<mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:20px&#x27;&gt;LoanOps on AWS — infrastructure + auth (build spec)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mohit Bohra | 2026-11-13 | v2 | Source of truth: &lt;code&gt;infra/terraform&lt;/code&gt; | Follow the teal numbers 1 → 16, then read the panels below" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=13;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1240" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;N&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; = step number (full text in Steps panel) &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;solid&lt;/b&gt; = request / data &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;dashed grey&lt;/b&gt; = token, control, registration &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#DD344C&#x27;&gt;red dashed&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; = TARGET, not built yet &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; arc = lines cross, not joined &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#ED7100&#x27;&gt;orange box&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; = the single ECS cluster" style="rounded=1;arcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EDF3FF;strokeColor=#007CBD;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1300" y="30" width="1940" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:16px&#x27;&gt;Steps — read in order&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Person opens LoanOps (browser) or connects Cursor. OneLogin login page; OneLogin checks the password against Active Directory.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; OneLogin hands the identity to Auth0 (SAML). Auth0 issues a signed user JWT.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;3.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Browser only: loads the React UI from CloudFront. CloudFront reads the private S3 bucket via OAC. Cursor skips this.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;4.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Client calls the &lt;b&gt;internal ALB&lt;/b&gt; over HTTPS with &lt;code&gt;Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;JWT&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. DNS from Route 53, TLS cert from ACM.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; ALB routes by path: &lt;code&gt;/chat* /eval* /pipelines* /health /mcp/tools*&lt;/code&gt; → agent-api :8000. &lt;code&gt;/mcp /mcp/* /ready&lt;/code&gt; → mcp-server :8001 (Cursor goes here directly).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;6.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color=&#x27;#DD344C&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TARGET:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; service verifies the JWT (Auth0 keys) and asks AppServices AppAuth: does this person + app have a LoanOps role? No role → 403. &lt;i&gt;Today: one shared token &lt;code&gt;MCP__AUTH_TOKEN&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;7.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Agent calls MCP tools at &lt;code&gt;mcp-server.loanops.local:8001&lt;/code&gt; (Cloud Map private DNS). Agent never goes back through the ALB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;8.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Agent asks Bedrock (LLM + embeddings) and stores chat sessions + vectors in Aurora.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;9.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; MCP finds the right API: capability graph in Neptune (SPARQL, IAM SigV4) + ApiIndex vectors in Aurora.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;10.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; MCP gets a bot token from the Auth0 M2M tenant (client credentials), cached until it expires.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;11.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; MCP calls the Plaisse API: &lt;b&gt;read-only GET&lt;/b&gt; with the bot token. Plaisse sees the LoanOps bot, not the person.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;12.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Answer + citations go back the same way. Logs → CloudWatch, traces → Langfuse.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;13.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; EventBridge Scheduler starts the pipeline task in the &lt;b&gt;same cluster&lt;/b&gt; (UTC): 02:00 EAKG nightly · 02:30 ApiIndex · 03:00 SOP ingest · Mon 06:00 audit.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;14.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Pipeline task pulls GitLab repos + OpenAPI specs and Confluence SOP pages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;15.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Pipeline writes Aurora (EAKG, ApiIndex, doc vectors) and Neptune (graph), then the task exits. No idle cost.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#007CBD&#x27;&gt;16.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Deploy: GitHub Actions assumes an IAM role via OIDC (no stored keys), pushes ARM64 images to ECR, updates the ECS services. Tasks read secrets from Secrets Manager at start." style="rounded=1;arcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#232F3E;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2100" width="1580" height="760" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="faq" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:16px&#x27;&gt;Infra decisions — questions answered&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Are all Fargate tasks in the same cluster?&lt;/b&gt; Yes. One ECS cluster per env: &lt;code&gt;loanops-&amp;lt;env&amp;gt;-cluster&lt;/code&gt;. Inside it: 2 always-on &lt;b&gt;services&lt;/b&gt; (agent-api, mcp-server) + 1 &lt;b&gt;scheduled task&lt;/b&gt; (eakg-sync) that 4 EventBridge crons launch. Separate task definitions, so each deploys and scales on its own. All share: ARM64 Graviton, runtime subnets, one ECS security group, one task IAM role, one log group.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why two services, not one?&lt;/b&gt; agent-api = chat brain (LLM, sessions). mcp-server = shared tool server for the Agent, Cursor and other MCP clients. Different callers, different scaling.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why is the pipeline task on Spot even in prod?&lt;/b&gt; Batch, safe to retry, not on the chat path. Chat path (agent + mcp) is On-Demand in prod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dev vs Prod&lt;/b&gt; (same Terraform, &lt;code&gt;env_name&lt;/code&gt; switches defaults)&lt;table border=&#x27;1&#x27; cellpadding=&#x27;4&#x27; style=&#x27;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;margin-top:4px&#x27;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;dev&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;prod&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;agent-api / mcp-server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1 task each · Fargate Spot&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2 tasks each · On-Demand · spread over runtime subnets (2 AZs)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;eakg-sync pipeline task&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Spot&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Spot&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Aurora min ACU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0 (pauses after 5 min idle)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.5 (no cold start)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Neptune&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1→2 NCU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1→2 NCU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Container Insights&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;off&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;on&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;ALB TLS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;HTTP :80 if no cert&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;set &lt;code&gt;acm_certificate_arn&lt;/code&gt; → HTTPS :443&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Network:&lt;/b&gt; corp VPC is discovered (&lt;code&gt;create_network=false&lt;/code&gt;), not created. ALB is internal (corp / VPN only). No public IPs on tasks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Security groups:&lt;/b&gt; ALB SG in 80/443 · ECS SG in 8000–8001 from ALB SG, 8001 from itself (Agent → MCP) · Aurora 5432 + Neptune 8182 only from ECS SG.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Secrets:&lt;/b&gt; one secret &lt;code&gt;loanops-&amp;lt;env&amp;gt;-app&lt;/code&gt;, injected at task start. Nothing secret in images or tfvars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Built vs target:&lt;/b&gt; built = every AWS box here + bot (M2M) calls to Plaisse + shared MCP token. &lt;font color=&#x27;#DD344C&#x27;&gt;Target&lt;/font&gt; = step 6 (per-person JWT + AppAuth). Later, optional: on-behalf-of so Plaisse sees the person.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Out of scope:&lt;/b&gt; no EC2, no NAT/public ingress, no write calls to Plaisse (GET only)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#232F3E;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1660" y="2100" width="1580" height="760" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
